- impl AppError placed beneath the enum in core/types.rs, per docs/CONTRACTS.md
  §1's own code fence (see PROGRESS.md D-011 for why PLAN.md's separate
  error.rs line in its Repository layout diagram does not apply here).
- code(): static per-variant match, unique by construction.
- message(): delegates to the Display impl thiserror generates from each
  variant's #[error("...")] string.
- remediation(): Some(..) for the nine variants with an actionable next
  step, None for the six that don't have one.
- every_app_error_variant_has_a_serialized_shape: one assertion per variant.
- no_variant_message_is_empty, code_values_are_unique_across_variants: both
  iterate a shared all_app_error_variants() fixture.
- core/mod.rs: #![deny(clippy::unwrap_used, clippy::expect_used)], scoped to
  core/ only (ipc/ doesn't exist yet -- see PROGRESS.md Observations).
- src-tauri/clippy.toml: allow-unwrap-in-tests / allow-expect-in-tests, so
  the deny doesn't also fire inside existing #[cfg(test)] code.
- PROGRESS.md: T-004 moved to In progress, D-011 recorded, two Observations
  recorded (db/migrations/mod.rs's expect() outside tests; ipc/mod.rs must
  copy the same clippy attribute when created).

No local Rust toolchain and no push access this session (same constraint as
T-001-T-003): nothing here has been compiled, formatted, clippy-checked, or
run. Handed to the owner as a patch.
